theory('Hashing In Strings | Theory', 'Polynomial hash represents a sequence by a modular weighted sum. Prefix hashes plus powers permit O(1) substring-hash calculation after O(n) preprocessing. Equal hashes do NOT prove equal strings: collisions exist. Double hashing reduces accidental collisions but does not make equality exact. For exact matching verify candidate characters or use KMP/Z. Java long multiplication may overflow before modulo; choose a modulus/base whose intermediate product fits, or use an overflow-safe multiply. Normalize subtraction modulo a positive modulus. A rolling hash removes the outgoing high-order digit, multiplies by base, and adds the incoming digit.')
add('Reverse every word in a string', '''    public static String solve(String s){ String[] words=s.trim().split("\\\\s+"); StringBuilder out=new StringBuilder(); for(int i=words.length-1;i>=0;i--){ if(words[i].isEmpty()) continue; if(out.length()>0) out.append(' '); out.append(words[i]); } return out.toString(); }''','System.out.println(solve("  the sky   is blue  "));','blue is sky the',
    'Interpret this sheet item as reverse WORD ORDER, retaining letters within words and normalizing whitespace.', 'Tokenize whitespace-delimited words, then append them in reverse index order with one separating space.', 'O(n) time and O(n) storage.', 'the,sky,is,blue -> blue,is,sky,the.', 'The title can also mean reverse letters within each word. This lesson explicitly states its word-order contract; use per-word reversal for the other variant.')
add('Minimum number of bracket reversals to make an expression balanced', '''    public static int solve(String s){ if(s.length()%2==1) return -1; int open=0,close=0; for(char c:s.toCharArray()){ if(c=='{') open++; else if(c=='}'){ if(open>0) open--; else close++; } else throw new IllegalArgumentException(); } return (open+1)/2+(close+1)/2; }''','System.out.println(solve("}{{}}{{{"));','3',
    'For a string of { and }, reverse individual braces to make it balanced; return minimum reversals or -1.', 'Cancel matched pairs. Remaining unmatched braces consist of closes then opens. Two closes or two opens need one reversal; odd leftover counts each need rounding up.', 'O(n) time; O(1) space.', 'After cancellation, compute ceil(unmatchedOpen/2)+ceil(unmatchedClose/2).', 'An odd total length can never balance. Parenthesis-type mixing requires a different contract.')
add('Count and say', '''    public static String solve(int n){ if(n<1) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); String s="1"; for(int step=1;step<n;step++){ StringBuilder next=new StringBuilder(); for(int i=0;i<s.length();){ int j=i+1; while(j<s.length()&&s.charAt(j)==s.charAt(i)) j++; next.append(j-i).append(s.charAt(i)); i=j; } s=next.toString(); } return s; }''','System.out.println(solve(5));','111221',
    'Starting at term 1="1", each next term describes runs of the previous term.', 'For every maximal run, append its length then its character. Runs partition the old term, producing one unambiguous next term.', 'O(sum of generated term lengths) time; O(max consecutive term lengths) memory.', '1 -> 11 -> 21 -> 1211 -> 111221.', 'n is one-based. Read a completed previous string; do not mutate it while discovering runs.')
lps_code = '''    public static int[] lps(String s){ int[] a=new int[s.length()]; for(int i=1,len=0;i<s.length();){ if(s.charAt(i)==s.charAt(len)) a[i++]=++len; else if(len>0) len=a[len-1]; else a[i++]=0; } return a; }'''
add('KMP Algorithm or LPS array',lps_code+'''\n    public static List<Integer> solve(String text,String pattern){ List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>(); if(pattern.isEmpty()){ for(int i=0;i<=text.length();i++) out.add(i); return out; } int[] fail=lps(pattern); for(int i=0,j=0;i<text.length();){ if(text.charAt(i)==pattern.charAt(j)){ i++; j++; if(j==pattern.length()){ out.add(i-j); j=fail[j-1]; } } else if(j>0) j=fail[j-1]; else i++; } return out; }''','System.out.println(solve("ababa","aba"));','[0, 2]',
    'Return all zero-based starts of pattern in text, including overlapping matches. Empty pattern matches every boundary.', 'LPS stores each prefix\'s longest proper prefix that is also suffix. On mismatch, fall back to that border rather than rechecking known characters. After a match, fall back to allow overlaps.', 'O(n+m) time; O(m) failure array plus output.', 'ababa contains aba at 0; after matching, keep border a and match again at 2.', 'Do not reset pattern index to zero after every full match; that loses the efficiency/border invariant.', 'Direct comparison at each start is O(n*m) worst time and O(1) auxiliary space.')
add('Z function', '''    public static int[] solve(String s){ int[] z=new int[s.length()]; int l=0,r=0; for(int i=1;i<s.length();i++){ if(i<=r) z[i]=Math.min(r-i+1,z[i-l]); while(i+z[i]<s.length()&&s.charAt(z[i])==s.charAt(i+z[i])) z[i]++; if(i+z[i]-1>r){ l=i; r=i+z[i]-1; } } return z; }''','System.out.println(Arrays.toString(solve("aaaaa")));','[0, 4, 3, 2, 1]',
    'z[i] is the longest prefix matching the suffix beginning at i; z[0]=0 by convention.', 'Maintain the rightmost prefix-matching box [l,r]. Inside it, reuse the corresponding earlier Z value capped at the box boundary, then extend comparisons beyond that boundary.', 'O(n) time; O(n) returned array, O(1) extra state.', 'aaaaa: from position 1 match four letters, then reuse progressively shorter box matches.', 'Index 0 has differing conventions; here it is explicitly zero. Use a separator absent from the alphabet for pattern+separator+text matching.')
add('Rabin Karp Algorithm', '''    public static List<Integer> solve(String text,String pattern){ final long mod=1000000007L,base=257; int n=text.length(),m=pattern.length(); List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>(); if(m>n) return out; if(m==0){ for(int i=0;i<=n;i++) out.add(i); return out; } long high=1,wanted=0,current=0; for(int i=0;i<m;i++){ wanted=(wanted*base+pattern.charAt(i))%mod; current=(current*base+text.charAt(i))%mod; if(i<m-1) high=high*base%mod; } for(int i=0;i<=n-m;i++){ if(current==wanted&&text.regionMatches(i,pattern,0,m)) out.add(i); if(i<n-m){ current=(current-text.charAt(i)*high%mod+mod)%mod; current=(current*base+text.charAt(i+m))%mod; } } return out; }''','System.out.println(solve("ababa","aba"));','[0, 2]',
    'Find all exact pattern matches, using rolling hashes as a filter and direct verification for collisions.', 'Compute the initial polynomial hash, then remove the outgoing character\'s contribution, shift by base, and add the incoming character. Matching hashes trigger exact regionMatches.', 'O(n+m+candidateCount*m) time; O(1) auxiliary space plus output. Worst case O(n*m), including repetitive true matches.', 'aba hash matches window 0 and window 2; both are verified before emitting.', 'Hash equality alone is not exact matching. Products fit long for this chosen base/modulus and UTF-16 alphabet.')
add('Longest happy prefix',lps_code+'\n    public static String solve(String s){ return s.isEmpty()?"":s.substring(0,lps(s)[s.length()-1]); }','System.out.println(solve("level"));','l',
    'Return the longest NONEMPTY proper prefix that is also suffix, or empty if none.', 'The final LPS entry is exactly the largest proper border length for the entire string.', 'O(n) time and O(n) failure-array space plus output.', 'level begins and ends with l, but no longer proper prefix matches its suffix.', 'The full string is not a proper prefix. Empty input has no nonempty border.')
add('Shortest Palindrome', '''    public static String solve(String s){ int[] a=new int[2*s.length()+1]; for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++) a[i]=s.charAt(i); a[s.length()]=-1; for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++) a[s.length()+1+i]=s.charAt(s.length()-1-i); int[] fail=new int[a.length]; for(int i=1,j=0;i<a.length;i++){ while(j>0&&a[i]!=a[j]) j=fail[j-1]; if(a[i]==a[j]) j++; fail[i]=j; } int palindrome=fail[a.length-1]; return new StringBuilder(s.substring(palindrome)).reverse().append(s).toString(); }''','System.out.println(solve("aacecaaa"));','aaacecaaa',
    'Add characters only at the FRONT to make a shortest palindrome. Input is ASCII/ordinary BMP characters, excluding surrogate-pair semantics.', 'Find the longest palindromic prefix via LPS on s, a unique sentinel, and reverse(s). The unmatched suffix must be mirrored in front; no shorter addition could cover it.', 'O(n) time/space.', 'Longest palindromic prefix is aacecaa; unmatched a is mirrored in front.', 'A literal separator might appear in input; integer sentinel -1 cannot equal a char value. StringBuilder.reverse handles surrogate pairs differently from the code-unit LPS, so the stated character contract matters.')
